<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!-- Coordinates for the routes, from the self-hosted geocoder: in the Action menu of the contacts. -->
    <record id="action_partner_locate" model="ir.actions.server">
        <field name="name">Locate on the map (routes)</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="base.model_res_partner"/>
        <field name="binding_model_id" ref="base.model_res_partner"/>
        <field name="binding_view_types">list,form</field>
        <field name="groups_id" eval="[(4, ref('group_route_manager'))]"/>
        <field name="state">code</field>
        <field name="code">action = records.action_bf_route_locate()</field>
    </record>
    <!--
        Where a contact's place on the map comes from. Until now the street fallback was
        invisible on the contact: the office could not tell a point the geocoder found from
        one accepted out of a position read at the door, and the second kind makes the gap
        shown on a stop stop being an independent check. Route managers only, like the
        action above.
    -->
    <record id="view_partner_form_bf_route" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">res.partner.form.bf.route.place</field>
        <field name="model">res.partner</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="base.view_partner_form"/>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//notebook" position="inside">
                <!-- ⚠️ The group goes on the PAGE, not on the view record: Odoo 18 refuses
                     an inherited view that carries groups_id of its own. -->
                <page name="bf_route_place" string="Place on the map (routes)"
                      groups="bf_route.group_route_manager">
                    <group>
                        <group string="Street point, for the plans">
                            <field name="bf_route_street_latitude" readonly="1"/>
                            <field name="bf_route_street_longitude" readonly="1"/>
                            <field name="bf_route_street_from_position" readonly="1"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>
                    <div class="text-muted small">
                        The street point is used to plan the kilometres when the contact has no
                        coordinates of its own. It never guides the phone. When the date above is
                        filled, the point was accepted from a position read on a route: the gap
                        shown at a stop of this customer then compares a reading with a reading,
                        and confirms nothing on its own.
                    </div>
                </page>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
